+# Design audit after Issues 935 and 936
+
+Audited on 2026-10-16 at main
+`465ff928c1f2ceb9f9b8f8084465475e45799ee8`, after PRs 937 and 938 merged.
+This record belongs to branch `audit/2026-10-16-post938`. It records an audit and
+issue publication, not implementation of the findings.
+
+The requested focus was type/enum boundaries, unnecessary backward compatibility,
+and duplicated state management. No compatibility adapter is required for future
+fixes. `software-design-philosophy` guided the evaluation; three independent
+read-only audits covered analyzer, runtime, and persistence. The coordinator
+inspected workspace/selection boundaries, checked the findings, and repeated the
+report-reader reproduction.
+
+## Evaluation
+
+**7.5/10: six of eight diagnostic rows supported in the inspected production
+boundaries.** This is a scoped design assessment, not a numerical guarantee about
+every source file or a performance score.
+
+| Diagnostic | Assessment | Evidence or remaining work |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Describe module responsibilities in one sentence | Pass | Core transitions, analyzer discovery, workspace ownership, process execution, and report/session I/O have distinct roles. |
+| Interfaces simpler than implementations | Pass | Effects/events, validated configuration, and private worker states hide substantial mechanisms. |
+| Change implementation without updating distributed assumptions | Partial; not counted | Synthetic outcomes, workspace ownership, and stopping rules still require synchronized updates. Issues 940–943 reduce these dependencies; 939 preserves typed-reader information at the boundary. |
+| Interface comments describe abstractions | Pass in inspected boundaries | Workspace operations describe ownership on failure; readers distinguish progress and review; runtime contracts describe acknowledgement and cleanup. |
+| Design is part of code review | Pass | Recent type/ownership changes and this audit include explicit scope, counterexamples and independent review. |
+| Modules own important design decisions | Pass | Core owns transition policy, workspace owns filesystem capabilities, report readers own structural validation. Local duplication within these owners remains actionable. |
+| Boundaries understandable without tracing every implementation | Pass at module level | Architecture/OKF contracts and boundary comments identify ownership and evidence limits. The report implementation currently violates its intended typed validation boundary. |
+| 10–20% of time invested in design improvement | Unmeasured; not counted | No time-allocation data was collected. Measure representative development work before awarding this row. |
+
+Reaching 10/10 requires eliminating the identified synchronization/reader-boundary
+problems and establishing the design-investment diagnostic with actual data.
+Adding more enums without reducing legal-state ambiguity would not improve the
+assessment.
+
+## Filed issues
+
+| Issue | Priority | Finding and bounded correction |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| [939](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/939) | Medium | Review decodes report configuration through `Value`, losing duplicate keys before typed validation. Preserve original field information until strict review decoding while retaining progress's opaque configuration contract. |
+| [940](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/940) | Medium | Synthetic statuses are broad `MutationStatus` values copied into worker states and output actions. Use a narrow synthetic outcome with one owner. |
+| [941](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/941) | Medium | Deadline, disk stop and cancellation repeat the same retirement/drain/finalization routing. Share the routing while preserving cause-specific outcomes. |
+| [942](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/942) | Medium | Active/pending workspace ownership is split across two maps and two completion Options despite exclusive production states. Use a slot enum and typed returned ownership. |
+| [943](https://github.com/HayaoSuzuki/hoimin/issues/943) | Low | `created_workers`, write-only `mutant_limit_reached`, and the mirror `records_written` counter carry no independent information. Remove exactly these fields without adding a shared abstraction. |
+
+Source locations are pinned in each issue. Principal files inspected were
+`crates/hoimin-core/src/{machine,resume,config,report}.rs`,
+`crates/hoimin-cli/src/workspace/{mod,operation,owned}.rs`,
+`crates/hoimin-cli/src/artifacts/run_report.rs`, and the analyzer modules including
+`store.rs`, fact indexes, callable imports and exception analysis.
+
+The live issue list contained only 570, 743 and 806 before publication, with no
+open PRs. The latest 100 closed issues were checked, including 856, 872, 895–902,
+911–916, 923–925, 929–931, 935 and 936. The new issues concern remaining code, not
+reopening completed work. The publication bodies contain acceptance conditions,
+compatibility decisions, verification scope and five review checks.
+
+## Report-reader reproduction
+
+The existing issue-936 binary was used, not a new audit-main build:
+
+- Binary: `.worktrees/issue-936/target/debug/hoimin`, version 0.10.0.
+- Checkout: clean `6894b3b17d4b335577b54d8614415397d5aabaf2`.
+- Binary SHA-256: `e83508d9b0cc081d2c3bba3db62ab1a0bac651757543785d6f852b678203ecc1`.
+- Compared with audit main, crate source differences are confined to analyzer
+  files. Relevant report reader, review and configuration code is identical.
+- Input: a schema-8 plan and schema-6 golden-report fixture adjusted to its
+  candidate/configuration. This was not a newly executed mutation test run.
+
+Scratch inputs are under `/private/tmp/hoimin-post938-report-decode-e0njhyst/`:
+`plan.json`, `valid.json`, `invalid-config.json`, and `duplicate-config.json`.
+Each case ran `hoimin review list PLAN --store absent.sqlite3 --report REPORT
+--format json` on macOS. The coordinator repeated all three cases independently.
+
+| Raw configuration field | Exit | Observation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
