+| `"import_roots":null` | 2 | `invalid type: null, expected a sequence` |
+| `"import_roots":null,"import_roots":[]` | 0 | Accepted; stdout byte-identical to the valid case |
+
+The store remained absent. The valid/duplicate stdout SHA-256 was
+`31ed1b2d1bc6286c01ec8185594fea4078b60d10d7ade35bc9cc62c5e2f34697`.
+The temporary result record is `/tmp/hoimin-post938-repro-results.json`.
+Issue 939 contains a portable raw-string mutation recipe. This establishes the
+reader acceptance difference, not a security exploit or normal-writer defect.
+
+## Counterexamples and deferred cleanup
+
+- `all_legacy()` remains a historical 43-operator helper used to assemble the
+  current default plus later additions. There is no runtime legacy-mode parser.
+  A future local cleanup can define the current allowlist directly and move old
+  subsets into test fixtures. It is lower value than the filed issues; do not
+  replace defaults with all operators and accidentally enable opt-in mutations.
+- Old report readers, DB migrations, alias names and omitted required-array
+  repair have already been removed by earlier work. No new reason was found to
+  reintroduce them. Current optional fields and raw CLI defaults are not
+  automatically backward-compatibility debt.
+- Git's `DiffPlan::Legacy` preserves global rename/unmerged-diff behavior and
+  handles path batching limits. Windows disposition fallback supports current OS
+  operations. Their names do not justify deleting them as format compatibility.
+- Analyzer fact indexes and exception indexes are deliberate derived caches.
+  Callable imports' trusted and possible provenance have distinct meanings.
+  Control-flow exits describe simultaneous abstract alternatives, not exclusive
+  runtime states. They should not be merged mechanically.
+- `HierarchyReport.emitted/ineligible` are unused accounting candidates, but too
+  small to justify a separate issue. Preserve the actual `SiteOutcome` distinction.
+- Exception-project string errors appear to lose cancellation classification, but
+  the cancellation-select/timeout paths mask ordinary public outcomes. No
+  observable failure was established, so no bug was filed.
+- Root cleanup readiness, namespace lifecycle, process cancellation gates, output
+  drain evidence, and process quiescence represent different observations or
+  ownership. Multiple fields alone do not establish redundant authority.
+- Persisted outcomes/diagnostics and independently useful event projections are
+  not removed simply because a narrow consumer reads only part of them.
+
+## Review and verification record
+
+Scope stage, five passes: (1) pinned latest main; (2) checked worktree and remote;
+(3) read architecture/knowledge contracts; (4) separated three independent audit
+domains; (5) excluded completed/open work and established no-compatibility scope.
+
+Finding stage, five passes: (1) checked declarations and every relevant reference;
+(2) traced producers, updates and consumers; (3) considered deliberate caches,
+projections and lifecycle distinctions; (4) bounded proposed changes and checked
+historical issues; (5) checked acceptance tests and the strength of evidence.
+Each delegated audit also reported five passes.
+
+Publication stage, five passes: (1) checked exact source links; (2) independently
+reviewed the issue drafts; (3) narrowed the spool requirement to stores whose
+pushes all succeeded, avoiding a new partial-write-recovery promise; (4) recorded
+binary provenance and repeated the report reproduction; (5) checked the live
+issue/PR list again and published only the five reviewed bodies.
+
+No Rust/Python production source was changed. No workspace suite, new proptest,
+new mutation campaign or Lean proof was run during this audit. The new issues
+specify where existing properties/oracles should be rerun during implementation.
+Native evidence here is limited to the macOS report-reader reproduction.
+Final documentation checks passed: 49 OKF pages parsed with reserved-file rules,
+local targets and catalog reachability; the updated architecture concept's
+source IDs/footnotes and this record's SHA/revision matched. Site generation and
+`git diff --check` passed. All five published issues were read back and their
+OPEN state, titles and complete bodies matched the reviewed drafts. No product
+source or tests were changed in this audit branch.
